WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
RelayPlan is a relief planning simulator.

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:05.500
This is the actual app.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.500
The default exercise has two depots, one hundred and eighty kits, and

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.700
three hundred kits of demand.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.350
All places and numbers are fictional.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.800
Start with the allocation planner.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.750
Every community receives sixty percent of its demand.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.250
Here are the exact counts and the unmet need.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.350
Now compare strategies.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.300
The nearest-first heuristic delivers the same number of kits, but Orchard

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.400
receives none.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.600
RelayPlan protects the lowest coverage, with more transport effort.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.100
That trade-off stays visible.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.600
Let's change North depot's stock.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.600
The plan recalculates immediately.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.600
Restore the sample, then open a route.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:54.300
Capacity and travel estimates are editable, and routes can be blocked.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.800
In Stress Test, preview closing South depot to Orchard.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.300
The lowest coverage falls from sixty to twenty-five percent.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.600
The preview leaves the original plan intact.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:11.400
Apply the closure to see the blocked route and revised allocations.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:15.000
Switch to a shortage exercise, then reset.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:18.800
Import a scenario to reproduce your own inputs.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.900
Invalid files show an error and keep the current plan.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:29.100
Export the allocation audit, exact community counts, or a reusable scenario.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.600
Files are generated locally.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:36.700
Finally, How it works explains the three objectives, the research and

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:37.900
the model's limits.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:42.550
We checked the solver against independent exhaustive enumeration.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:48.000
This is a learning and tabletop prototype, not a live dispatch system.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:53.500
RelayPlan makes each shortfall visible, so a person can review the decision.
